  "description": "K-05 v1.15, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1295: the lead's ruling on v1.12's open gap 62, DL-535's reading (d); ADR-016 section 5; DL-753's R5 (b)). It only adds to v1.14 (data-access.v1.14.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to every earlier version down to v1): every v1.14 definition is here under its own name, by reference, save the five restated: readTesterStanding.request, readTesterStanding.response and personStanding.response, each for its text (README items 68 and 69: the rows that make a person a tester), with personStanding.response also holding that a team member is a tester, and readTesterStanding.exchange and personStanding.exchange, to refer to them. So every v1 to v1.14 exchange is a v1.15 exchange. Widened: readTesterStanding (item 68) and personStanding's tester (item 69) read, beside the live K-36 v1 team row, a live listing in K-22 v1.3's staging_testers, where staging's human testers are listed apart from Rosie's team (build prompt 9.4: no team row, so no page reaches them), each answering with the same fields. No request or answer gains a field, and no state, move or call is added; the reads take K-22 v1.3's new table (its migration is the database engineer's card). Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
